  <p>With AI, the need for trust is so much more important, because you've got actors acting as humans where they're not. We need a way to verify information. We need a way to authenticate humanity. I need a way to have an authenticated representation of myself on the blockchain, that it's 100% me doing it — not a copy of me or a clone of me. Blockchain is a method. Maybe there's a better method, I don't know. But it's a method we've invented that can manage authentication and prevent falsifying information. For me it's a necessary feature of using AI safely, as we have to have trust in data.</p>
